    "readout_text": "To determine the **acute angle** formed by two lines with slopes $ m_1 = 2 $ and $ m_2 = \\frac{1}{3} $, we use the formula for the angle $ \\theta $ between two lines:\n\n$$\n\\tan(\\theta) = \\left| \\frac{m_2 - m_1}{1 + m_1 m_2} \\right|\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Plug in the values\n\n$$\n\\tan(\\theta) = \\left| \\frac{\\frac{1}{3} - 2}{1 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\right|\n$$\n\nSimplify the numerator and denominator:\n\n- Numerator: $ \\frac{1}{3} - 2 = \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{6}{3} = -\\frac{5}{3} $\n- Denominator: $ 1 + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{3}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{5}{3} $\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\tan(\\theta) = \\left| \\frac{-\\frac{5}{3}}{\\frac{5}{3}} \\right| = \\left| -1 \\right| = 1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the angle\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\tan^{-1}(1)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\theta = 45^\\circ\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{45^\\circ}\n$$\n\nThis is the **acute angle** formed by the two lines.",
